1. SATURATION (SLUSE66A Equation 2, printed page 85: Isat at least ICHG plus half the ripple): the worst peak above is
   9.74 A against Isat 25.4 A (804-1 p.1, typical, the 30 percent drop): 38 percent of it. At that current the
   inductance has fallen to about 91 percent of its zero-current value on 804-2's curve (INFERRED).
2. RMS (804-1 p.1 note 6): the worst RMS above is 8.00 A against 17.5 A (20 C rise) and 24.0 A (40 C rise), 46 percent
   of the first; the copper loss there is at most 0.37 W (DCR 5.70 mOhm maximum). The rating is Coilcraft's reference
   figure on its own board; the rise on board A is a layout item.
3. RIPPLE (Equation 3 and the boost ripple, page 85; TI's guidance 20 to 40 percent of the maximum charge current): at
   400 kHz and the nominal inductance the ripple reads 1.16 to 2.44 A over the envelope, 15 to 31 percent of 7.936 A;
   at 340 kHz with the inductance 20 percent low it reads up to 3.62 A. TI pairs 4.7 uH with 400 kHz (Table 9-4, page 27).
4. A FAULT BOUND: the converter's input over-current comparator trips at 150 mV across R16B, 15.0 A of input current
   (8.5, VOCP_lim_ACX, page 15); in boost mode the inductor carries the input current, so at most 15.0 A; in buck mode
   the inductor's average current is the input current times VIN over VOUT, at most 21.0 A at 16.8 V into 12.0 V. Both are
   under the typical Isat; Coilcraft prints no minimum Isat and calls the saturation soft (804-1 p.1), so this is not a
   bound on a part at its worst. The buck leg's low-side OCP (VOCP_lim_Q2, 150 mV across Q8B) depends on the FET's
   RDS(on) and is not used here.
CORE LOSS: not in any of the above. 804-1 p.1 prints none ("Core and winding loss: See www.coilcraft.com/coreloss"),
and no held Coilcraft document gives a figure or a loss model; see records/s119/README.md for the public search.
END.
